\begin{bgproofidea}[title={Two subsequences close in on the same number}]
With decreasing \(b_n\to0\), even partial sums move in one direction and odd partial sums in the other. Their difference is the next term magnitude, which tends to zero, so both subsequences converge to the same limit.
\end{bgproofidea}

\begin{bgvisual}{u4a-alternating-partial-sums}{Alternating partial sums bracket the limit}{When alternating term magnitudes decrease to zero, odd and even partial sums approach the same value from opposite sides.}
