\section*{Common Errors in Sequence and Series Problems}
\begin{bgmistake}[title={Do not confuse necessary with sufficient}]
The condition \(a_n\to0\) is necessary for \(\sum a_n\) to converge, but it is not sufficient.
\end{bgmistake}
\begin{bgmistake}[title={Do not compare in the useless direction}]
Being smaller than a divergent series proves nothing; being larger than a convergent series proves nothing.
\end{bgmistake}
\begin{bgmistake}[title={Do not forget endpoint tests}]
A power-series radius settles the open interval only. Endpoints are separate series problems.
\end{bgmistake}
